From c4bf691bf01880493c25ebed3c96ce61477a951b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 14:00:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] perf(gateway): dispatcher tick reads profile names
 only and each other board once

hermes-hub gateway, 600 s at 118% of a core with 12 boards (2026-11-12 13:34Z):
- _receipt_scope ran list_profiles() twice per board per tick: config and gateway
  liveness for every profile, only to take the names (7.6% of samples). It now
  uses list_profile_names().
- count_running_tasks_other_boards opened every other board from every board's
  tick: 132 connections per tick (6.4%). Inside kanban_board_share.tick_counts()
  (one dispatcher tick) a board's count is kept until that board's own tick
  asks, so later boards still see the workers it started; 22 connections.
  Outside a tick every call reads every board, as before.

Review notes from #1406:
- gateway_names does not memoise the answer of a failed hub.db read.
- repair_divergence skips a row that left the replica mid-pass instead of
  aborting the pass with KeyError.

Tests: tests/hermes_cli/test_dispatcher_tick_read_budget.py (5 of 7 fail on the
old code: 20 opens vs budget 8, profile probes, remembered failure, KeyError).
